{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "The Natural World"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "The Animal World"}, {"type": "position", "content": 10}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 12}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Identify and describe events in a range of social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Asking for Clarification and Emphasizing a Point"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you want more information from someone, you can use <span class=\"strong\">embedded questions</span>. <br/><br/>You can emphasize a point by asking <span class=\"strong\">rhetorical questions</span>. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Embedded questions</span> are questions within other questions or statements. Often, you use the phrases <span class=\"italic\">Do you know ... </span>, <span class=\"italic\">Do you remember ... </span>, <span class=\"italic\">Can you tell me ...</span> , <span class=\"italic\">Can you show me ...</span> to start an <span class=\"strong\">embedded question</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For Example:<br/>  <span class=\"strong\">Direct question</span>: <span class=\"italic\">What are you trying to say?</span><br/> <span class=\"strong\">Embedded question</span>: <span class=\"italic\">Can you tell me what you are trying to say?</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can also use <span class=\"strong\">rhetorical questions</span> to emphasize a point. <br/>Rhetorical questions are questions that don't need to be answered. They are said when the speaker wants to express their feelings about a situation. The speaker does not expect the listener to actually give an answer. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "  For example: <br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">What are you going to do? </span>(when there is nothing to be done) <br/><span class=\"italic\">How about that?</span> (when you want to make a point)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Can you clarify what you're trying to say?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'm not sure what you're trying to tell me."}, {"type": "example", "content": "How's that working for you?"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to forward"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to send an e-mail to a further destination"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I forwarded you an online brochure I got the other day."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le12ob10aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about nature."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Showing That You Understand Someone's Feelings"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "In conversation, one way to keep the conversation going is to show empathy. This means showing that you understand the other's person's feelings or situation. You use <span class=\"strong\">must</span> followed by an adjective when you want to empathize with someone. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">must</span> and an adjective (either in it's ED or ING form). When you use the -ED form, it refers to the feelings that a person has. When you use the -ING form, it refers to the thing that is causing feelings.<br/><br/>For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">You must be delighted.<br/> You must be nervous.<br/> They must be surprised!<br/> It must be terrifying to do that!<br/><br/>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Your work must be exciting!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "You must be bored with your job right now."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn7le12ob10re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "offender "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " a person who commits a crime"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This helps to ensure offenders cannot escape punishment."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le12ob10aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to endeavour"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to try hard to do or achieve something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Our officers endeavor to protect threatened animals and plants."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "e